What is Spring Configuration XML?

Spring Configuration XML is an XML file used to define Spring Beans and configure their dependencies. The Spring IoC (Inversion of Control) Container reads this file during application startup, creates the required objects, injects dependencies, and manages their lifecycle.

Advantages
Centralized bean configuration.
No need to manually create objects using new.
Supports Dependency Injection.
Makes applications easier to maintain and modify.
Important XML Tags
Tag/Attribute	Purpose
<beans>	Root element containing all bean definitions.
<bean>	Defines a Spring-managed object (Bean).
id	Unique name used to retrieve the bean.
class	Fully qualified class name of the bean.
<property>	Sets property values using setter injection.
name	Specifies the property name.
value	Assigns a value to the property.
<constructor-arg>	Passes values through the constructor.
scope	Defines bean scope (singleton, prototype, etc.).
ApplicationContext

ApplicationContext is the main interface of the Spring IoC Container.

Responsibilities
Reads XML configuration.
Creates bean objects.
Injects dependencies.
Manages the lifecycle of beans.
Provides beans using getBean().
ClassPathXmlApplicationContext

ClassPathXmlApplicationContext is an implementation of ApplicationContext that loads XML configuration files from the classpath.

